            <ArticleTitle>[Depression and elevation of the ST segment in the V4R lead during the stress test of a patient with a proximal lesion of the right coronary artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>440-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a patient with a proximal right coronary artery lesion in whom opposite shifts of ST segment in V4R lead were observed during and after exercise. ST-segment depression was provoked by exercise, while ST-segment elevation appeared in the recovery phase. We speculate that different degrees of myocardial ischemia (non-transmural vs transmural) may explain this apparently paradoxical response.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
